# Fernly page objects

## 1. Where locators live

Put every `getByRole`, `getByLabel`, and `getByText` on a class under `tests/pages/`. Specs orchestrate flows and assert; they do not define selectors.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — tests/e2e/browse.spec.ts
const browse = await new BrowsePage(page).goto();
await browse.selectSort('price-desc');
await expect(browse.plantCardTitle(browse.firstPlantCard())).toHaveText(THAI_MONSTERA_NAME);

// ❌ BAD — selector in the spec
await page.getByLabel('Sort by').selectOption('price-desc');
await expect(page.getByRole('article').first().getByRole('heading', { level: 3 })).toHaveText(name);
```

## 2. Locator order (role, label, text)

Prefer accessible queries in that order. Do not use CSS classes, test ids, or XPath in page objects.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — tests/pages/BrowsePage.ts
this.sortBy = page.getByLabel('Sort by');
this.plantsCountHeading = page.getByRole('heading', { level: 2, name: /\d+ plants/ });

// ❌ BAD
this.sortBy = page.locator('.SortSelect-module__select');
this.firstCard = page.locator('article').first();
```

## 3. Unnamed controls on a card

When a control has no accessible name (the heart save toggle), find it by role inside its card and comment why.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — tests/pages/BrowsePage.ts
/** Save (heart) toggle — icon-only button with no accessible name; scoped by card + button role. */
saveButtonInCard(card: Locator): Locator {
  return card.getByRole('button');
}

// ❌ BAD
saveButton = page.locator('button.PlantCard-module__save');
```

## 4. Actions and assertions

Page object methods perform navigation and interaction only. They return `void`, `this`, or the next page object — never call `expect`. Keep every assertion in the spec.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — tests/pages/BrowsePage.ts
async selectSort(value: string): Promise<BrowsePage> {
  await this.sortBy.selectOption(value);
  return this;
}

// ❌ BAD — assertion in a page object
async selectSort(value: string): Promise<void> {
  await this.sortBy.selectOption(value);
  await expect(this.firstPlantCard()).toContainText('Monstera');
}
```
